//@ compile-fail

// A function and an extension method need a body. `std/src/builtins.bd` writes the compiler-provided methods as
// declarations without bodies for the tools, and the compiler never loads that file, so in a program the missing
// body is an error (`spec/stdlib.md`, "Compiler-known types").

fn twice(x: i32): i32 //~ E0001
fn List<T>.second(self): Option<T> //~ E0001

fn main() {
    println("{}", twice(2))
}
